  "notes": "Uber Mission Bay 3 & 4, 1655 & 1725 3rd St -- two 11-story, LEED Gold office towers (combined ~584,000-586,208 sq ft, sources disagree on the exact figure) developed by a joint venture of Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Uber Technologies and the Golden State Warriors, designed by SHoP Architects, completed 2021. Grouped as one record: the two towers' airspace-condo office units (blklots 8722063 for 1655 3rd and 8722087 for 1725 3rd) share one identical underlying land parcel polygon in DataSF's own parcel map (confirmed by exact geometry match), the same kind of single-underlying-parcel situation as Pier 70's historic-core grouping precedent -- not two separately mapped footprints. 1725 3rd St directly adjoins Chase Center. As of 2025 SEC filings, Uber still lists 1725 3rd St as its corporate HQ address, though a 2023 report said that specific building had never been fully staffed and was being marketed for sublease -- current occupancy is genuinely unclear and not resolved here.",
